      "id": "lru-implementation-uses-sidecar-not-value-shape-change",
      "summary": "Plan §3.4.3 prescribes `self.indexed_ready.evict_lru(min_floor)` without specifying internal representation. The implementation adds a sidecar `last_access: DashMap<Arc<str>, u64>` to IndexedReadyDb rather than changing the value type from `Arc<IndexedReady>` to `(tick, Arc<IndexedReady>)`, preserving pointer-equality on cached entries (which `unchanged_live_file_never_re_lowered_across_publish_cycles` directly relies on via Arc::ptr_eq). Choice rationale: changing the value type would break ~30 call sites that store/load Arc<IndexedReady> directly, and the discriminating test's pointer-equality assertion is a stronger correctness guarantee than the LRU compute path.",
      "files": ["crates/verter_session/src/project_type_store.rs"]
    },
    {
      "id": "min-floor-is-method-parameter-not-config-field-read",
      "summary": "Plan §3.4.3 pseudocode says `self.indexed_ready.evict_lru(self.config.eviction.min_floor)`, implying ProjectTypeStore knows about HostConfig. Final design passes `min_floor: usize` as a parameter to `evict_unreachable_indexed_ready` because ProjectTypeStore does not own a HostConfig (the host does); callers derived from `host.config().eviction_policy.min_floor` pass the value through. Rationale: keeps ProjectTypeStore HostConfig-free per the layering convention; HostConfig stays the single owner of policy, ProjectTypeStore is the mechanism.",
      "files": ["crates/verter_session/src/project_type_store.rs"]
    }
